"GIW", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Describing the role of client in computing"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: \n<span class=\"bullet\">Proofread the sentence.</span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Click on the incorrect word.</span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Type in the correct word to complete the sentence.\n</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>\n"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 9}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob11re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Describing types of clients "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le02ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span> I'm going to ask Karl to design a wiki. I'm thinking we can ask him to add client in computing to the wiki he designed last month because we're focusing on servers, computer hardware and computer software. I'm going to talk to him this afternoon, and I want to ask you to work with him. I'm going to send you a document with key information; we must include the concept of client in computing, the types of clients there are; and you should also include its role in computing. But first, can we discuss what this is before I leave? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Philip: </span> Sure. I'm talking about client in computing in our next meeting, so I read some articles about the subject. I can tell you that a client is a computer hardware or software that sends a request to a server to access a specific service. This server is usually on another computer system.</br>"}, {"time": "50500", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span> What types of clients are you talking about in the meeting?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Philip: </span> I\u2018m going to explain that we can have fat, thin, and hybrid clients. Fat clients perform the bulk of any data processing operations by themselves, and they don't rely on a server. We should think of personal computers as an example of this type of clients. Then we have thin clients, which use the resources of the host computer and normally present only processed data that they receive from an application server. We can think of web applications such as Office Web Apps as an example. Finally, I'm talking about hybrid clients which combine the previous types of clients.  They should process information locally, but rely on the server for storing certain data. We can think of video websites as an example of a hybrid client.</br>"}, {"time": "106000", "image": "enpe8n3le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span> I must leave soon, could you quickly explain the role of the client in computing?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Philip: </span>Sure, the primary function of a client-server system is to create a division of labor between a centralized server and the individual computers that are running your software. This helps businesses to create and process intensive applications. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Manager: </span> Thank you! Let me know if you have to include extra information about the company in the wiki. <br/>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le02ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}